{"version":3,"kind":"Article","sha256":"39d38f58ae16c40da3be5bb03db1063e2d2715a2977dcab9cacdba0607de006c","slug":"introducing-the-technical-notes","location":"/articles/introducing-the-technical-notes/introducing-the-technical-notes.md","dependencies":[],"frontmatter":{"title":"Introducing the Technical Notes","description":"The writing on this site that people want to cite now has its own series. A technical note is written like a short paper, gets an archival PDF, and carries a DOI that resolves to it.","keywords":["Underworld Code"],"authors":[{"nameParsed":{"literal":"Louis Moresi","given":"Louis","family":"Moresi"},"name":"Louis Moresi","orcid":"0000-0003-3685-174X","affiliations":["Australian National University"],"id":"contributors-introducing-the-technical-notes-generated-uid-0"}],"affiliations":[{"id":"Australian National University","name":"Australian National University"}],"date":"2026-08-14","license":{"content":{"id":"CC-BY-4.0","url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","name":"Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International","free":true,"CC":true}},"open_access":true,"github":"https://github.com/underworld-technical-notes/underworldcode.org","source_url":"https://github.com/underworld-technical-notes/underworldcode.org/blob/main/articles/introducing-the-technical-notes/introducing-the-technical-notes.md","edit_url":"https://github.com/underworld-technical-notes/underworldcode.org/edit/main/articles/introducing-the-technical-notes/introducing-the-technical-notes.md","exports":[{"format":"md","filename":"introducing-the-technical-notes.md","url":"/underworldcode.org-preview/18c8c99505/build/introducing-the-tech-84516b71d5ec6dc43227b2ad734dd4a9.md"}]},"mdast":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"block","children":[{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":17,"column":1},"end":{"line":22,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Our underworld web site has always carried two kinds of writing. Some of it is news — a\nrelease, a workshop, a paper accepted. The rest is the sort of thing a reader\nlater wants to point at: how a solver behaves, what a benchmark\nmeasured and what it demonstrates, why a method works the way it does and\nwhere it stops working. The two have been mixed together, and there has been\nno way to cite the second kind.","position":{"start":{"line":17,"column":1},"end":{"line":17,"column":1}},"key":"rHhOGPJJlP"}],"key":"AJtFoQepz8"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":24,"column":1},"end":{"line":28,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"So we now have ","position":{"start":{"line":24,"column":1},"end":{"line":24,"column":1}},"key":"hnt2Q2LqmQ"},{"type":"strong","position":{"start":{"line":24,"column":1},"end":{"line":24,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"technical notes","position":{"start":{"line":24,"column":1},"end":{"line":24,"column":1}},"key":"yfdK7P21d8"}],"key":"kWtw9xjp5G"},{"type":"text","value":" that are written like a short\npaper or perhaps a preprint. Each one carries a version, an archival PDF built from the same source as the\npage, and a DOI that resolves to that PDF. Deposit is deliberate rather than\nautomatic: a note is published here first, and only gets an identifier when we\ndecide it is worth one.","position":{"start":{"line":24,"column":1},"end":{"line":24,"column":1}},"key":"FZIduekMjJ"}],"key":"wGml02UCHb"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":30,"column":1},"end":{"line":33,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"The point is for us to write down what we have created with enough content\nto be useful and not a lot more, and then refer to it — from a paper, from an\nissue, from the next note; instead of describing it again. Not quite\ndocumentation and not yet a research publication.","position":{"start":{"line":30,"column":1},"end":{"line":30,"column":1}},"key":"obdgpktzlr"}],"key":"TFJWvHveMf"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":35,"column":1},"end":{"line":39,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"The first two are up: ","position":{"start":{"line":35,"column":1},"end":{"line":35,"column":1}},"key":"kwx6ca0Erh"},{"type":"link","url":"/moving-the-mesh-without-remaking-it/","position":{"start":{"line":35,"column":1},"end":{"line":35,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Moving the Mesh Without\nRemaking It","position":{"start":{"line":35,"column":1},"end":{"line":35,"column":1}},"key":"WytDH9qqtx"}],"urlSource":"/moving-the-mesh-without-remaking-it/","key":"p9e9Z5ugAw"},{"type":"text","value":", on redistributing mesh\nnodes to follow the physics without remeshing, and ","position":{"start":{"line":35,"column":1},"end":{"line":35,"column":1}},"key":"YtdfNVQNAH"},{"type":"link","url":"/running-underworld-in-a-browser/","position":{"start":{"line":35,"column":1},"end":{"line":35,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Running Underworld in a\nBrowser","position":{"start":{"line":35,"column":1},"end":{"line":35,"column":1}},"key":"cCF16UsGau"}],"urlSource":"/running-underworld-in-a-browser/","key":"iAqL4zFmfj"},{"type":"text","value":", on launching any repository at any\nversion without installing anything.","position":{"start":{"line":35,"column":1},"end":{"line":35,"column":1}},"key":"OQ2CgmOpuD"}],"key":"acClbbCuqY"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":41,"column":1},"end":{"line":42,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Everything written before is still here, at the same addresses. The fifty posts\nthat already carry DOIs keep them, and those DOIs still resolve.","position":{"start":{"line":41,"column":1},"end":{"line":41,"column":1}},"key":"PbUgFmqMAQ"}],"key":"PncZYLkVO2"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":44,"column":1},"end":{"line":46,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"If you work with Underworld and have something worth writing down, the notes\nare open to you — ","position":{"start":{"line":44,"column":1},"end":{"line":44,"column":1}},"key":"DU2kaHBkh